戈培尔还允许向公众分发配套的传单，但将数量限制在2000份。他禁止在广播中发布公告，因为他不希望消息传出柏林。戈培尔有自己的想法来确保城市女性乘客的安全。他要求男性志愿者在晚上护送独自乘坐Yes Barn的女性。唯一可以申请此角色的男性是纳粹党准军事派系的成员，他们通过暴力手段强制执行政权。

71
00:47:48.000 --> 00:48:34.000
These men were referred to as brown shirts, named after the colour of their uniform. To be given the role of a brown shirt was considered an honour reserved for trustworthy men with no criminal record. The Minister of Propaganda's strategy appeared successful. As lone female passengers were escorted on the Yes Barn by brown shirts, the remainder of January passed with no further incidents. Mother of three, 39-year-old Johanna Voight stood alone at the Rumorsborg train station. It was 10pm on Tuesday, February 11, and Johanna was nervous.
这些人被称为“褐衫军”，以他们制服的颜色命名。被授予褐衫军的角色被认为是一种荣誉，仅限于没有犯罪记录的可靠男性。宣传部长的策略似乎奏效了。随着独自乘坐Yes Barn的女性乘客由褐衫军护送，一月的剩余时间里没有再发生任何事件。三个孩子的母亲，39岁的约翰娜·沃伊特独自站在鲁默斯堡火车站。那是2月11日星期二晚上10点，约翰娜很紧张。

72
00:48:34.000 --> 00:49:12.000
She knew about the Yes Barn murderer, and given she was pregnant, Johanna feared for the safety of her unborn baby. Her worry must have been palpable, because an experienced brown shirt approached having spent the day assisting women on their travels. Typically, women had to check in as part of the programme, and a brown shirt would then be authorised by Joseph Goebbels himself to personally escort her. Johanna hadn't made any such arrangements, but she asked the brown shirt if he would be willing to accompany her to Karlshorst station.
她知道Yes Barn杀手的事，而且考虑到她怀孕了，约翰娜为未出生婴儿的安全感到担忧。她的担忧一定是显而易见的，因为一名经验丰富的褐衫军走过来，他那天一直在协助女性出行。通常，女性必须作为计划的一部分进行登记，然后褐衫军会得到约瑟夫·戈培尔本人的授权来亲自护送她。约翰娜没有做任何此类安排，但她询问那名褐衫军是否愿意陪她去卡尔斯霍斯特车站。

73
00:49:12.000 --> 00:49:58.000
Although he'd already clocked off, Karlshorst was only one station away, so the man agreed. The pair entered the empty second-class compartment and took a seat. As the train took off and gained momentum, the brown shirt suddenly pulled an iron rod out from his jacket sleeve and immediately struck Johanna in the head with it. He then dragged her unconscious body to the door of the train and pushed her out. Johanna survived the initial attack, but by the time she was found, she'd succumbed to her injuries. There was nothing amongst Johanna's belongings that hinted towards her killer's identity.
虽然他已经下班了，但卡尔斯霍斯特只有一个站的距离，所以那个人同意了。两人进入空荡荡的二等车厢并坐下。当火车启动并加速时，褐衫军突然从夹克袖子里掏出一根铁棒，立即击中了约翰娜的头部。然后他把她失去知觉的身体拖到火车门口并把她推了下去。约翰娜在最初的袭击中幸存下来，但当她被发现时，她已经因伤势过重而死亡。约翰娜的随身物品中没有任何暗示凶手身份的线索。

74
00:49:58.000 --> 00:50:38.000
Rather, it was the absence of a certain item that gave investigators pause. Like several of the other victims, Johanna Voigt had been travelling on the S-Bahn without a ticket, an offence punishable by fine. While measures were in place to prevent people from riding the S-Bahn without a valid ticket, it was to be expected that the odd passenger would slip through without pain. However, it struck investigators as odd that so many of the murder victims were riding freely. Given it was highly unlikely that all of them had managed to avoid crossing paths with a
相反，正是某件物品的缺失让调查人员停了下来。像其他几名受害者一样，约翰娜·沃伊特在没有票的情况下乘坐S-Bahn，这是一种可处以罚款的违法行为。虽然已经采取了措施防止人们在没有有效车票的情况下乘坐S-Bahn，但偶尔有乘客溜过去也是意料之中的。然而，让调查人员感到奇怪的是，这么多谋杀受害者都是免费乘车的。鉴于她们所有人都不太可能成功避开

75
00:50:38.000 --> 00:51:14.000
ticket inspector, investigators developed a theory. If the killer was a current or former S-Bahn employee or posing as one, he could approach his victims without causing alarm. Some of the victims could have been lured onto the train with the promise of a free and safe journey. Alternatively, the killer could have confronted the women under the guise of checking their tickets before launching an attack. Curiously, Geda Kagoe recalled that her attacker had approached her shortly before she boarded
检票员，调查人员提出了一个理论。如果凶手是现任或前任S-Bahn员工，或者冒充员工，他就可以在不引起警觉的情况下接近受害者。一些受害者可能被承诺免费且安全的旅程而诱骗上车。或者，凶手可能在发动袭击前以查票为幌子与这些女性对质。奇怪的是，格达·卡戈回忆说，她的袭击者在登上S-Bahn前不久接近了她，并指引她去二等车厢。

76
00:51:14.000 --> 00:51:55.000
the S-Bahn and directed her to the second-class compartment. Considering he was dressed in uniform, she assumed he was a railroad employee and obeyed his command without question. Elizabeth Bendoff had also been told to board the second-class compartment by a uniformed man shortly before her attack. Yet, both women clarified that he wasn't impersonating a ticket inspector. The S-Bahn was staffed by employees of the National Railroad, whose uniforms included a hat adorned with an eagle clutching a swastika.
考虑到他穿着制服，她以为他是铁路员工，便毫无疑问地服从了他的命令。伊丽莎白·本多夫在袭击前不久也被一名穿制服的男子告知要登上二等车厢。然而，两位女性都澄清说，他并没有冒充检票员。S-Bahn由国家铁路的员工配备，他们的制服包括一顶装饰着鹰抓万字徽章的帽子。

77
00:51:55.000 --> 00:52:38.000
Given that this matched witness descriptions of the killer, police had initially considered whether the offender could be a railroad worker. The problem was that there were over 5,000 uniformed employees of the National Railroad spread across 28 departments, so narrowing down the suspect list would be no easy feat. Roughly a quarter were eliminated immediately based on survivors' descriptions. The rest had to be questioned in addition to having their work schedules collated, checked and verified. Geda Kagoe and Elizabeth Bendoff were shown thousands of photos of men who worked for
鉴于这与目击者对凶手的描述相符，警方最初考虑该罪犯是否可能是铁路工人。问题在于，国家铁路有超过5000名穿制服的员工分布在28个部门，因此缩小嫌疑人名单绝非易事。大约四分之一的人根据幸存者的描述被立即排除。其余的人除了需要接受询问外，他们的工作时间表还必须进行整理、核对和验证。格达·卡戈和伊丽莎白·本多夫被展示了数千张为

78
00:52:38.000 --> 00:53:17.000
the S-Bahn, but neither woman recognized their attacker. 8,000 people who lived around the Friedrichsfelder Gardens were also looked into. Under pressure from Josef Goebbels to solve the case, hundreds more undercover and uniformed police officers were tasked with riding the S-Bahn and manning the key train stations along the way. With no distinguishing features to be on the lookout for, they questioned every man they came across. Every train platform and compartment was diligently searched for any evidence of the killer's
S-Bahn工作的男性的照片，但两人都没有认出她们的袭击者。居住在弗里德里希斯费尔德花园周围的8000人也受到了调查。在约瑟夫·戈培尔要求破案的压力下，数百名卧底和穿制服的警察被派往乘坐S-Bahn并驻守沿途的关键火车站。由于没有明显的特征可寻，他们询问了遇到的每一个男人。每一个火车站台和车厢都被勤奋地搜查，寻找任何凶手存在的证据，

79
00:53:17.000 --> 00:54:00.000
presence, which sometimes required entire sections of the train line to be shut down. Police were finally able to publish a more detailed newspaper article about the case, this time revealing that multiple women had been killed. They further increased the reward on offer to 13,000 Reichsmarks for information pertaining to Johanna Voigt's murder or any of the previous attacks, while warning women against riding in the second class compartment. The article also detailed the possibility that the offender was wearing a national railway uniform or something similar.
这有时需要关闭整段铁路线。警方终于能够发表一篇关于此案的更详细的报纸文章，这次透露有多名女性被杀。他们进一步将悬赏金额提高到13000帝国马克，以征集有关约翰娜·沃伊特谋杀案或之前任何袭击的线索，同时警告女性不要乘坐二等车厢。文章还详细说明了罪犯可能穿着国家铁路制服或类似服装的可能性。

80
00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:43.000
Police were inundated with roughly 1,500 tips from the public. While none of the tip-offs led to the identification of the perpetrator, the heavy-handed investigation had seemingly brought an end to his killing spree. By Thursday, July 3, 1941, five months had passed since the S-Bahn murderer had a last strike. With the increased police presence and the public now on high alert, commuters were safer than ever before. In the early morning hours, 35-year-old Frieda Kotsio wrote the S-Bahn without incident.
警方收到了大约1500条来自公众的线索。虽然没有任何线索能锁定罪犯，但高压调查似乎结束了他的杀戮狂潮。到1941年7月3日星期四，距离S-Bahn杀手最后一次作案已经过去了五个月。随着警察力量的增加和公众的高度警惕，通勤者比以往任何时候都更安全。在清晨，35岁的弗里达·科齐奥乘坐S-Bahn时没有发生任何意外。

81
00:54:43.000 --> 00:55:22.000
She disembarked at Ruhmersburg station along with nine other women and one man. As they left the platform, the group scattered to take their different routes home. Frieda headed alone down a path towards the nearby allotment gardens. Once she reached the quiet and darkened grounds, she was struck in the back of the head with an iron bar. The beating continued once she was on the ground, resulting in Frieda's skull caving in. Her attacker then tore off her clothing below the waist and proceeded to rape her before
她在鲁默斯堡车站与另外九名女性和一名男性一起下车。当他们离开站台时，这群人分散开来，各自走回家的路。弗里达独自沿着一条小路走向附近的配给花园。当她到达安静而黑暗的场地时，后脑勺被铁棒击中。当她倒在地上时，殴打仍在继续，导致弗里达的头骨塌陷。她的袭击者随后撕掉了她腰部以下的衣服，并在逃离现场前强奸了她。

82
00:55:22.000 --> 00:56:02.000
fleeing the scene. Frieda's bloodied and partially naked body was found shortly after, making her the eighth fatality at the hands of the S-Bahn murderer. Frieda's death was a blow to investigators. Having narrowed in on the S-Bahn, they'd overlooked the perpetrator's previous hunting grounds and hadn't thought to put safety measures in place in the allotment gardens. The police felt partially responsible for Frieda Kotsio's murder, as it was clear that the killer knew the police had taken over the train system.
弗里达血迹斑斑且半裸的尸体不久后被发现，使她成为S-Bahn杀手手中的第八名受害者。弗里达的死对调查人员是一个打击。在将重点缩小到S-Bahn后，他们忽视了罪犯之前的狩猎场，也没有想到在配给花园采取安全措施。警方对弗里达·科齐奥的谋杀案负有部分责任，因为很明显，凶手知道警方已经接管了火车系统。

83
00:56:02.000 --> 00:56:44.000
Instead of changing tactics to flush him out, their defiant actions had forced the killer away from the very spot they might have otherwise caught him. Still, the gardens provided evidence that the S-Bahn did not. A set of fresh shoe prints were pressed in the dirt surrounding Frieda's body and led 50 meters beyond, indicating that someone had knelt down next to her body and inspected it before running from the scene. Plaster molds of the prints revealed the shoeing question was a size 39.5 with an extra thick rubber sole and distinctive tread pattern.
他们强硬的行动并没有改变策略来引诱他出来，反而迫使凶手离开了他们本可以抓住他的地方。尽管如此，花园确实提供了S-Bahn没有的证据。弗里达尸体周围的泥土中印着一串新鲜的鞋印，并延伸到50米外，表明有人在逃离现场前曾跪在她的尸体旁检查过。鞋印的石膏模型显示，该鞋的尺码为39.5码，带有超厚橡胶底和独特的胎面花纹。

84
00:56:44.000 --> 00:57:25.000
They matched shoes manufactured by a specialist podiatry company. As luck would have it, the company kept well-documented records of all their customers, including those who had purchased the size 39.5 shoe. Armed with this list, investigators began tracking down and interviewing each of the customers. Investors were fighting in the war or lived too far away and were promptly ruled out. But there was one man that caught investigators' interest. He lived near the Rumorspaw train station, right by the allotment gardens where dozens
它们与一家专业足病公司制造的鞋子相匹配。幸运的是，该公司保存了所有客户的详细记录，包括那些购买了39.5码鞋子的客户。拿着这份名单，调查人员开始追踪并采访每一位客户。调查人员有的在战争中服役，有的住得太远，很快被排除。但有一个人引起了调查人员的兴趣。他住在鲁默斯堡火车站附近，就在几十名

85
00:57:25.000 --> 00:58:06.000
of women had been attacked. He was a carpenter named V. Hyman. A check of his police records revealed that Hyman had a criminal conviction for voyeurism, having previously been caught spying on a couple having sex. It was the only blemish on an otherwise clean record. Hyman was taken in for questioning, during which he denied involvement in any of the Esban murderers' crimes. In the meantime, his home was searched for any evidence that could link him to the case.
女性遭到袭击的配给花园旁边。他是一名名叫V·海曼的木匠。对他警察记录的检查显示，海曼曾因偷窥罪被定罪，此前曾被抓到偷窥一对夫妇发生性关系。这是他原本清白的记录中唯一的污点。海曼被带去审讯，期间他否认参与了任何S-Bahn杀手的罪行。与此同时，他的家被搜查，寻找任何可能将他与此案联系起来的证据。

86
00:58:06.000 --> 00:58:44.000
Investigators found a pair of custom podiatry shoes, and compared them to the molds taken alongside Frida Kotziol's body. They were a match. When Hyman was informed of this discovery, he admitted that he'd stumbled across Frida's body and had knelt down to inspect it. Once he realized she was dead, he fled the scene. Hyman didn't admit to this earlier because he was scared of being used as a scapegoat. He was also mindful that the penalty for sex-based crimes were severely amplified during the
调查人员发现了一双定制的足病鞋，并将它们与在弗里达·科齐奥尸体旁采集的模型进行了比较。它们是匹配的。当海曼被告知这一发现时，他承认他偶然发现了弗里达的尸体，并跪下来检查。一旦意识到她已经死了，他就逃离了现场。海曼没有早点承认这一点，因为他害怕被当作替罪羊。他还意识到，在灯火管制期间，性犯罪的惩罚被严重加重了。

87
00:58:44.000 --> 00:59:51.000
blackout. Given his history as a convicted sex offender, he feared that he'd be handed a death sentence despite his innocence, just so authorities could close the case. Police were forced to drop the Hyman lead when they discovered that he had solid alibis for a large percentage of the Esban murderers' attacks, thus ruling him out as the perpetrator. Whether he'd face any repercussions for failing to report Frida Kotziol's murder remained to be seen. Whatever the case, police were back to square one.
鉴于他作为性犯罪者的前科，他担心即使自己是无辜的，也会被判处死刑，只是为了让当局结案。当警方发现海曼在S-Bahn杀手的大部分袭击中都有可靠的不在场证明时，他们被迫放弃了海曼这条线索，从而排除了他是罪犯的可能性。他是否会因未报告弗里达·科齐奥的谋杀案而面临任何后果还有待观察。无论如何，警方又回到了原点。

88
00:59:51.000 --> 01:00:47.000
Following the murder of Frida Kotziol, police extended their covert surveillance to the Friedrichsfelder allotment gardens, while also observing the Esban more discreetly. Although these preventative measures had previously deterred the perpetrator temporarily, the police knew they were unsustainable in the long term. Once officers were forced to return to other duties, the Esban murderer would no doubt resume his spree. Meanwhile, investigators were still making their way through the long list of employees from the National Railroad, questioning everyone about the murders.
在弗里达·科齐奥被谋杀后，警方将秘密监视范围扩大到了弗里德里希斯费尔德配给花园，同时也更谨慎地观察S-Bahn。虽然这些预防措施此前曾暂时阻止了罪犯，但警方知道从长远来看它们是不可持续的。一旦警察被迫返回其他职责，S-Bahn杀手无疑会恢复他的狂潮。与此同时，调查人员仍在处理国家铁路员工的长名单，询问每个人关于谋杀案的情况。

89
01:00:47.000 --> 01:01:30.000
One so far had raised their suspicions and the ticket inspector lead was a dead end. Police considered the possibility that the killer wasn't a railroad employee at all, but had been wearing a fake or stolen uniform. Then, a week after the murder of Frida Kotziol, as they were wrapping up close to six months' worth of railroad employee interviews, there seemed to be a much needed breakthrough. Police concluded the interviews with a standard question. Have you noticed anything suspicious about any of your co-workers? One man had.
到目前为止，有一个人引起了他们的怀疑，而检票员的线索是一条死胡同。警方考虑了凶手根本不是铁路员工，而是穿着假制服或偷来的制服的可能性。然后，在弗里达·科齐奥被谋杀一周后，当他们结束了近六个月的铁路员工采访时，似乎出现了一个急需的突破。警方以一个标准问题结束了采访：你有没有注意到你的同事有什么可疑之处？有一个人注意到了。

90
01:01:30.000 --> 01:02:14.000
He'd spotted a colleague, 28-year-old Paul Ugozov, leaving work in the middle of his shift by jumping over a fence. When confronted, Ugozov said he was off to see a woman. He returned some time later without any of his superiors noticing his absence. Ugozov had worked for the railroad for six years, having worked his way up from a temporary role as a manual laborer to a permanent position as an auxiliary signalman. He was stationed in a tower near the Rumsburg station, where he worked mostly alone, monitoring signalling that ensured the trains ran efficiently and safely.
他发现一名同事，28岁的保罗·乌戈佐夫，在轮班中途跳过栅栏离开工作岗位。当被质问时，乌戈佐夫说他要去见一个女人。他在一段时间后回来，没有任何上级注意到他的缺席。乌戈佐夫在铁路工作了六年，从体力劳动的临时工一路晋升为辅助信号员的固定职位。他驻扎在鲁默斯堡车站附近的一座塔楼里，大部分时间独自工作，监控确保火车高效安全运行的信号。

91
01:02:14.000 --> 01:03:01.000
Despite having worked at the company for a long time, Ugozov wasn't close to his colleagues. Many didn't even know his name. Paul Ugozov had already been questioned in relation to the S-Bahn murders. Records showed he had been working at the time of the attacks, and his role had him positioned in a signal tower, a building along the railroad that was independent of the stations. He was not required to ride the S-Bahn as part of his duties or interact with passengers. Officers had found Ugozov assiduous and industrious, and he was praised by his superiors for his unblemished work history.
尽管在公司工作了很长时间，但乌戈佐夫与同事并不亲近。许多人甚至不知道他的名字。保罗·乌戈佐夫此前曾因S-Bahn谋杀案受到询问。记录显示他在袭击发生时正在工作，他的角色使他驻扎在信号塔里，这是一座独立于车站的铁路沿线建筑。他不需要作为职责的一部分乘坐S-Bahn或与乘客互动。警官们发现乌戈佐夫勤奋刻苦，并因其无瑕的工作记录受到上级的称赞。

92
01:03:01.000 --> 01:03:41.000
He was ultimately ruled out of the investigation. However, when his colleague reported Ugozov's history of disappearing mid-shift, his roster no longer provided him with an alibi. While Ugozov didn't have a violent criminal record or history of sexual deviancy, he had been arrested for burglary some years prior. Even with this conviction, there was nothing in Ugozov's background to suggest he was capable of the S-Bahn murderers' crimes. He was a hard-working German national and married father of two.
他最终被排除在调查之外。然而，当他的同事报告乌戈佐夫轮班中途消失的历史时，他的排班表不再为他提供不在场证明。虽然乌戈佐夫没有暴力犯罪记录或性变态史，但他几年前曾因入室盗窃被捕。即使有这个定罪，乌戈佐夫的背景中也没有任何迹象表明他有能力犯下S-Bahn杀手的罪行。他是一名勤奋的德国公民，也是两个孩子的已婚父亲。

